cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CAUSA: Causal Agency and Utterance-State Alignment"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - alias: Stell
    name: Stell
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-3291-0679"
repository-code: "https://github.com/stell2026/causa"
abstract: >-
  Two metrics for whether an artificial agent's outputs are causally tied to
  its own internal state: directional ownership, which scores agreement
  between a predicted and an observed state change, and expression
  congruence, which scores alignment between an expressed state and the
  internal state it was expressed from. Includes permutation baselines for
  distinguishing a real effect from an artefact of the state space.
keywords:
  - sense of agency
  - machine consciousness
  - cognitive architecture
  - predictive processing
  - evaluation metrics
